## https://github.com/tj/git-extras/blob/main/Commands.md
Abort current revert,rebase,merge or cherry-pick,without the need to find exact command in history           | git abort
Define,search and show aliases                                                                               | git alias
Creates a zip archive of the current git repository                                                          | git archive-file
Populates the file matching authors/contributors -i with the authors of commits                              | git authors
Opens the current git repository website in your default web browser                                         | git browse
Opens the current git repository CI website in your default web browser.                                     | git browse-ci
Operations that execute on multiple git repositories                                                         | git bulk
Pretty listing of branches sorted by the date of their last commit                                           | git brv
Generates a changelog from git(1) tags (annotated or lightweight) and commit messages                        | git changelog
Does a hard reset and deletes all untracked files from the working directory, including those in .gitignore  | git clear
Does a hard reset and deletes all untracked files from the working directory, excluding those in .gitignore  | git clear-soft
Add a co-author to the last commit                                                                           | git coauthor
List commits since date (defaults to "last week")                                                            | git commits-since
Continue current revert,rebase,merge or cherry-pick,without the need to find exact command in history        | git continue
Output author's contributions to a project                                                                   | git contrib
Output commit count                                                                                          | git count
Copy a file to another one keeping its history and allowing for merge conflicts handling                     | git cp
Create local branch name                                                                                     | git create-branch
Delete local and remote branch name                                                                          | git delete-branch
Deletes branches that are listed in git branch --merged                                                      | git delete-merged-branches
Deletes branches that have been "squashed-merged" into a specified branch                                    | git delete-squashed-branches
Delete submodule name                                                                                        | git delete-submodule
Delete local and remote tag name                                                                             | git delete-tag
Lists files that differ from another branch                                                                  | git delta
Displays "effort" statistics                                                                                 | git effort
The main git-extras command                                                                                  | git extras
Create/Merge the given feature branch name                                                                   | git feature
Reset its contents to a clone of the remote                                                                  | git force-clone
Fork the given github <repo>                                                                                 | git fork
Create empty local branch                                                                                    | git fresh-branch
Clone repository into a subdirectory of the configured path                                                  | git get
Sets up the gh-pages branch                                                                                  | git gh-pages
Merge commits from src-branch into dest-branch                                                               | git graft
Calculate the change in blame between two revisions                                                          | git guilt
Generate sample gitignore file from gitignore.io                                                             | git ignore-io
Too lazy to open up .gitignore                                                                               | git ignore
Show information about the repo                                                                              | git info
List all commits on the local branch that have not yet been sent to origin                                   | git local-commits
Lock a local file filename                                                                                   | git lock
List local locked files                                                                                      | git locked
Commits changes with a generated message                                                                     | git magic
Merge branch into                                                                                            | git merge-into
Merges two repository histories                                                                              | git merge-repo
Print out which commits are on one branch or the other but not both                                          | git missing
Checks out a merge request from GitLab                                                                       | git mr
Completely remove a file from the repository,including past commits and tags                                 | git obliterate
Sends commits to a pastebin site using pastebinit                                                            | git paste
Checks out a pull request from GitHub                                                                        | git pr
Rebase a branch on top of another using a merge commit and only one conflict handling                        | git psykorebase
Create pull request via commandline                                                                          | git pull-request
Rewrite history to change author's identity                                                                  | git reauthor
Given you have a patch that doesn't apply to the current HEAD                                                | git rebase-patch
Release commit with the given <tag> and other options                                                        | git release
Rename a branch locally,and sync to remote via git push                                                      | git rename-branch
Rename a file or directory and ensure Git recognizes the change                                              | git rename-file
Rename a tag (locally and remotely)                                                                          | git rename-tag
Rename a git remote regardless of name conflict                                                              | git rename-remote
Git read-eval-print-loop                                                                                     | git repl
Reset one file to HEAD or certain commit                                                                     | git reset-file
Show the path to root directory of git repo                                                                  | git root
A convenient way to copy files from the current working tree to the working directory of a remote repository | git scp/rscp
Run grep as directed but replace the given files with the pattern                                            | git sed
Set up a git repository (if one doesn't exist),add all files,and make an initial commit                      | git setup
Show all branches merged in to current HEAD                                                                  | git show-merged-branches
Show the decorated graph view of one liner summarized commits from all branches                              | git show-tree
Show all branches not merged in to current HEAD                                                              | git show-unmerged-branches
Stamp the last commit message                                                                                | git stamp
Merge commits from src-branch into the current branch as a single commit                                     | git squash
Recall what you did or find what someone else did in a given range of time                                   | git standup
Outputs a repo or path summary                                                                               | git summary
Sync local branch with its remote branch                                                                     | git sync
Call touch on the given file,and add it to the current index. One-step creation of new files                 | git touch
Remove the latest commit                                                                                     | git undo
Unlock a local file filename                                                                                 | git unlock
Change files modification time to their last commit date                                                     | git utimes
Undo a Work In Progress(WIP) commit and put all of those changes back into the working directory             | git unwip
Create a Work In Progress(WIP) commit,which will include all changes in the working directory                | git wip